      "writtenOn": "2025-08-05T17:41:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Todd\u0027s comment about dropping vendorhook implementation details applies here as well. \n\nBut after reading the commit message, I\u0027m a little confused on how this wouldn\u0027t break things.  If you have many fair tasks on the rq, but the first up is a \"root\" privileged task, this implementation would cause you to schedule idle, when there are possibly a number of runnable tasks. This seems like it would allow a single root task to, in effect, cork the run-queue on that CPU.  Am I missing some detail?\n\nIt seems like you would want to deactivate the problematic selected task, and try to pick again from the rq to choose something else?",
      "revId": "737fd41e4377248c201bf2507fcab542d2d718a7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2481e287_d8a4895d",
        "filename": "kernel/sched/core.c",
